WEBVTT

00:00:00.673 --> 00:00:02.328
Cross text connections.

00:00:02.328 --> 00:00:03.923
One sentence per author.

00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:05.009
Then compare.

00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:08.244
Here's how to spot one.

00:00:08.244 --> 00:00:10.819
Two short texts on the same topic.

00:00:10.819 --> 00:00:14.165
And a question about how one author would respond to the other.

00:00:15.193 --> 00:00:18.319
It's testing whether you can track two viewpoints at once.

00:00:19.402 --> 00:00:20.677
Here's the method.

00:00:20.677 --> 00:00:23.177
Summarize Text 1 in one sentence.

00:00:23.177 --> 00:00:25.877
Summarize Text 2 in one sentence.

00:00:25.877 --> 00:00:30.597
Name the relationship: agree, disagree, or partly agree.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:33.895
Then answer for the exact point the question asks about.

00:00:34.973 --> 00:00:36.648
Listen for these clues.

00:00:36.648 --> 00:00:40.513
It is true that, followed by but, means partial agreement.

00:00:40.513 --> 00:00:44.488
Whatever they intended concedes one point, and moves to another.

00:00:44.488 --> 00:00:47.263
Text 2 rarely rejects everything.

00:00:47.263 --> 00:00:51.597
Often, the authors agree on the facts, but disagree about the cause.

00:00:52.626 --> 00:00:53.926
Let's try one.

00:00:53.926 --> 00:00:56.676
Text 1 says learning music improves math.

00:00:56.676 --> 00:00:58.301
Music is the cause.

00:00:58.301 --> 00:01:01.901
Text 2 says it's true that young musicians excel at math.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:04.226
But we can't say music is the cause.

00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:07.776
So Text 2 agrees on the pattern, and questions the cause.

00:01:07.776 --> 00:01:09.526
A is too extreme.

00:01:09.526 --> 00:01:12.776
C is wrong, because Text 2 accepts the data.

00:01:12.776 --> 00:01:15.556
D agrees with the conclusion of Text 1.

00:01:15.556 --> 00:01:16.597
B matches.

00:01:17.648 --> 00:01:19.973
Watch out for total disagreement.

00:01:19.973 --> 00:01:24.253
The authors usually clash on one specific point, not on everything.

00:01:25.311 --> 00:01:27.191
Here's the lesson on one page.

00:01:27.191 --> 00:01:28.266
How to spot it.

00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:29.666
The four steps.

00:01:29.666 --> 00:01:30.721
The clues.

00:01:30.721 --> 00:01:31.746
And the trap.

00:01:31.746 --> 00:01:34.511
Pause the video now, and copy it into your notes.
